    <td>
<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Ultima Online 2 - UO2 Vault After Chat for 9/27/2000</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>[Sanctum-Centar]</b> Ubiq, is your team considering the idea of "group" or "ritual" magic as a component of the game?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Sanctum- we're considering complimentary magic, which should be more fascinating.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We have a party system similar to EQ and UO's, but with some extra goodies.
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> ubiq when do the magic screenshots come out?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] soon, soon.
<br>
<br><b>[TWD]</b> Ubiq: In the Large fight in logos,t he 2 headed ogre hit the warrior, but the warrior didnt recoil, is that going to be put in later? recoils when hit or being thrown backwards?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> TWD] Recoils are already in.  How good they look will depend on circumstances.  Latency prevents true soul-calibre style fighting
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> But we do have reactionary combat.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: Will we even be able to have player run towns
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Sanctum] let's get housing back in first and then I'll worry about towns. =)
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Ubiq what plans do you have for money sinks in the game, so money is still somewhat useful at high lvls?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] we have several plans, I'll talk about them more as we get closer to implementing them.
<br>
<br><b>[Gonj]</b> What I wanna know is how well is a player-run economy gonna work out without housing?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Gonj] I think it will work very well.
<br>
<br><b>[autoexec]</b> with all the experience you have, have you figured out the perfect housing system? or is it imposible to prevent late players to never own a house (ie uo1)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> autoexec] we think we have a good plan.
<br>
<br><b>[Astalder]</b> Ubiq, what kind of continuity will UO2 have after release?  Sadly we saw a lot of disappointments in the area of updating and mainting the original UO.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Astalder] I think it will do very well.  We designed the architecture first and foremost to be expandable and stable, which means the live team can spend relatively little time fixing things
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> And relatively a lot of time progressing things.  If the live team uses this to it's full potential, ORIGIN will be 2 or 3 times as rich a year after it's been live.
<br>
<br><b>[Thor]</b> Ubiq: will you be playing a NPC, like Richard Garriott played Lord British?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Thor] Not planning on it.  I don't have the time to spend playing a character on 20 copies of a world and have a meaningful impact on the story. =)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Ahriman has created a set of characters which are designed to progress the story, and yes, be interacted with, in events.
<br><b>[Thor]</b> Ubiq: You could make guest apperances :-)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Thor] Then people will complain that I don't log in enough. =)
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Ubiq how many spells are in the game?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] more than 100+, but our system for adding new ones will be ridiculously easy.
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Will there be a one character server?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kallanar] too soon to tell.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> Ubiq; do you play UO ?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo]  Not for a very long time.
<br>
<br><b>[Orion]</b> Can we brube the Dev team with .3Mountain Dew?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Orion]  The team is actually partial to mountain dew.  I'm a Dr. Pepper man myself.
<br>
<br><b>[Tchrin]</b> Will we get to see the Particle system in action anytime soon?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Tchrin]  Soonish.  No promises tho.
<br>
<br><b>[TWD]</b> Ubiq: will it be one character per shard? will there be a name filter?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> TWD]  No comment yet.  Yes.
<br>
<br><b>[FireKnight]</b> Ubiq I just wonder how big will be the Ultima2 world in humans size?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Fireknight]  It takes 3 times as long to walk from Yew to Britain, and we have 3 continents instead of one.  does that give a rough idea?
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Ubiq have u ever played Legends of kesmai?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] Not in ages.
<br>
<br><b>[Vandal|UO2News]</b> why don't you have this souped-up "Dr. Pepper" and then like... start working on Prostitution as an in-game system :)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Vandal]  Why waste time coding systems that players can do in game without any code support? =)
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Will the seasonal changes be noticable or the land look the same?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] too soon to tell.
<br>
<br><b>[Pemolis]</b> Might as well ask this.  I know that I am going to get stuck if I bring a bunch of people into a dungeon and none of them can't pick locks.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Pemolis]  We try not to make only one path through a dungeon.
<br>
<br><b>[Vandal|UO2News]</b> And unless you're keeping a dark, dark secret, fornication isn't one of the skills you can learn?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Vandal] what you come up with in your sick imagination is more likely better and more gratifying than anything we could animate anyway.
<br>
<br><b>[FireKnight]</b> Wil UO2 work good enough with 56k and a crapy video card?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Fireknight] 56K modem should be fine.  Video Card is worth investing in a good one.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: How big is the world of New Sosaria compared to EQ or AC??
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex, dunno, haven't compared our world directly with them.  We're probably smaller than AC's landscape, but that's a conscious decision to not make more world than we could make interesting.
<br>
<br><b>[FireKnight]</b> Ubiq what video card do you think is the best for UO2?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> FireKnight] our graphics team is a big fan of nVidia products, so I'd suggest starting there.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Radeon performs very nicely too
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> hehe UBiq; do you perfer questions about the game or questions about the dev team and your likings?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] I prefer questions about questions.
<br>
<br><b>[Pemolis]</b> Might as well ask again.. Will we half to camp 1 spot and pull npc's one at a time to gain EXP?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> pemolis] our spawning system is random, so that shouldn't be possible, sorry.
<br>
<br><b>[Darkon]</b> UBIQ]</b> Will there be lots of funny lines to the AI of the NPC's heh Orcs calling you a newbie :)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Darkon] Ahriman has quite a sense of humor (if you can call it that), so expect some lines that are supposedly humorous. =)
<br>
<br><b>[Kaladon]</b> Medwynd: on some of the screenshots i saw a letter icon with a stamp... what does that mean?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kaladon] Those are temporary place holder icons
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kaladon] Depending on with what we ship with all art is subject to change
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> DO they curse in the game? Anyways why is there an R rating for the game?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] the game is not yet rated
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Talyn]</b> Ubiq: Could you expand a little on how your name filter will work, what type of names can you have?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Talyn] we're not going to be nazis about it, but our name filter will obviously kick out people who try to name themselves after a god, or a GM, or use certain words, etc, etc, etc
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> "gods" = Dev Team, sorry for the misunderstanding.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> §§Ubiq§§-would it be possible to emulate an origin shard... just like one of UOs?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] dunno
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] we don't officially support player shards, of course.
<br>
<br><b>[iio]</b> have you decided on the number of character slots per shard per account?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> iio] not yet.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: Will there be a REAL underground? Like caves and tunnels that go on forever and maybe even link town to town?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex] there will be caves.  They will go deep.  They will link different parts of the world.
<br>
<br><b>[Logo]</b> How are you planning to handle econmy problems like so many other games have failed at before
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Logo] that's always a place of experimentation.  We have a number of money sinks planned that should handle that quite tidily though.
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Ubiq: is xp gained from damage to or death of the monster?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] Death of.  Damage to is exploitable.
<br>
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> Ubiq, you know that little UO-faire typing thing going on Seattle? Is that going to be official like the Texas one, or is it like an unofficial one?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> The one in seattle is unofficial, being run by stratics I believe.
<br>
<br><b>[Lord_Berek_Halfhand]</b> Software process? How about something intereestin! like... Ubiq... What density will the overal landscape have? As far as trees, and animals and thigns... EQ was pretty barren
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Lord_berek] there's a reason for this.  For one thing, it takes a lot of time to build that much content
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> For another thing, both their game and our game has to save a lot of polys for the monsters and other characters.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> You only have a limited budget for polies, and you have to decide as a developer how you want to spend it.  We decided to focus our energy on cahracter customization.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> _§§Ubiq§§_what is your feelings on Horizon's lack of funds?(happy about less competitors or sad at the loss of a potential loss to the mmorpg world)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] last i heard they got funding again.
<br>
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> Ooh, I got a question... Ubiq, if we are able to swim, will it be as annoying as it was in Ultima 9?  (Like zooming out on your character forcing you to go into 1st person mode etc etc)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Baastuul, I'll do what I can to ensure our eventual solution isn't annoying.
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Ubiq can meers or humans climb trees?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Tree-climbing not currently in the plans.
<br>
<br><b>[TWD]</b> Ubiq: will something like fighting under water be able to be implemented after release of the game if it doesnt go in before release
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> TWD: anything can be implemented after release.  However, needless to say, we will have a limited set of resources, so what we can actually do will be limited.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We will try to choose the best possible priorities, with the help of the fans.  
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> ubiq]how can I go about getting on the origin team(game tester or some minor data filler guy) if I alrdy know c++, and some other programing language... better yet how did you come from no name guy to head
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] I proved myself to someone who mattered. 
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> UBIQ: Were you the same Ubiq in EQ beta with the superhigh Shaman character??
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex] no.
<br>
<br><b>[Orion]</b>  got one, who will get into the betas and how?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Orion] I can't comment on that one and do it justice.  That is up to Usul and Ravana.
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Ubiq name me one new cool spell :P plzz plz plz :)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] "Heartwrencher"
<br>
<br><b>[Horizons]</b> Ubiq..:.. Q:"What does UO2 have that other games don't?" A:"We're shipping" Is that the ONLY unique thing UO2 has going for it?? The hell kinda answer was that??
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Horizons] I gave a long answer to that question.  Feel free to scroll back and read it. =)
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Zeo]</b> Ubiq] hehe well um what position do you suggest to try and go for at the start of your programing carrer....
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] Three things.  1) build a portfolio of whatever you do best.  2) Make contacts.  3) get into the industry any way you know how.  Usually QA or CS.
<br>
<br><b>[Horizons]</b> They got 6 WHOLE sets of armor. I don't think my RAM will be able to support that =(
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Horizons] we have hundreds of pieces of clothing, all of which smoothly deform, show hued skin properly underneath, and hue correctly themselves.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Trust me, our character customization will be the bomb.
<br>
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> Ubiq, how will we take screenshots in UO2?  Hehehe
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Baastuul] we should have an ingame screenshot maker, but you can always do a alt-printscreen.
<br>
<br><b>[autoexec]</b> Ubiq: in the screenshots, we see towns and plains, but all seem to be empty around (not alot of trees etc). Will there be limitations to what will be on the landscape?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> autoexec] Many of our area which are coming on line now or very much more fleshed out
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Most of those screenshots were taken before areas had been populated with flora.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: Will clothes and robes billow and have mass or be skintight?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex] still too early for fully flowing clothes but not everything is skintight.  Check out the woman in the green dress.
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Ubiq:what kind of transportation do meers, humans and jukans have?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Viper] its too early to talk about that, since we don't have mounts.  However, when we do have mounts and vehicles, they likely won't be race limited.
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> ubiq: What will keep tech from over powering magic?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] it will be a balancing act.  We have a plan in palce.
<br>
<br><b>[Canis]</b> how does it feel to create your own game? You must love it
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Canis] it's exhilirating beyond belief.
<br>
<br><b>[Kaladon]</b> Medwynd: i know this isnt your field.. but can you tell me some of the dishes a cook can make?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kaladon] Sorry dont know that myself :)
<br>
<br><b>[Horizons]</b> Ubiq..:.. So if I go out a kill 20 people, the "system" will make it so that the next person that comes along with a butter knife will hack my arms and legs off??
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Horizons] Windy is better suited to talk about that system, but your description sounds inaccurate.
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Ubiq: will carpentry be useful in the game without houses?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] unsure.
<br>
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> You seem pretty big on Dasha.  She do somthing special?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Aviak] I'm a sucker for redheads.
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Ubiq: do you have plans to keep the bridge of fish?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] LOL. Um. No.
<br>
<br><b>[Orion]</b> Ohoh!!! big questioN! can you magically enchant a Blunderbuss?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Orion] Good q for mobius.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Talyn]</b> Ubiq: Can we get blue humans in uo2...please?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Talyn] I'll keep it in mind.
<br>
<br><b>[Yoda]</b> QUESTION - Why would any of the old PVP players that  left uo after the dread days want to play uo2? Is there anything in it for them? Or is osi still catering to the masses?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Yoda] We are focusing our PK part of the game on PVP instead of Mindless PK.  If what you find fun is randomly ganking newbies,
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> You will not like ORIGIN much.  If you like fighting for purpose, honor, revenge, and all that good stuff,
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We may well be the game for you.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> I wrote a good letter on the topic on the UO2 site, I recommend reading it.
<br>
<br><b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> UBIQ: will there be race wars?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Race Wars] I don't like race wars, since most people ignore them (see everquest).  Fundamentally, if you're a Meer and your friend is a Juka, I don't want to rpevent you from playing together.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Will there be politics and tension?  yes.  Will there be deep story?  Yes.  And it will be a lot deeper than "Jukans hate Humans".
<br>
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> And then there's flying....
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Aviak] no plans for flying immediately. 
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: Has yout team thought or implemented multi-person quests or spells?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex] there will be spell 'combos', or spells that compliment other spells, which is different than a 'ritual', but is more flexible and a lot easier to code. =)
<br>
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> Ubiq --- I have a more, er, serious question.. it might have been answered but I have not seen it yet, so I was wondering about logging off and the delay.  Say we're in level 4 of Dungeon Deceit and we have to get offline/off the computer for some reason (and seeing as we cannot gate or recall out of there), how will that be dealt with?  I don't want my char to sit there for 5 minutes, prone to any attacks by monsters while I am away from my character!
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Baastuul] still answering that question.
<br>
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> heh, flying is totaly unneeded i ment.  Swiming should be priority on that realm, than think about flying....
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Aviak] you can't do flying until you do swimming, or else things get messy when you plummet from the sky into the ocean =)
<br>
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> WHO HERE THINKS THEY SHOULD RELEASE A GOLD EDDITON PROTIONAL VIDEO!?
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> Like the first one, only in sterio, and higher rez!
<br><b>[Aviak]</b> Or make a Grim Faeries music video
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Aviak] we actually helped the Grim Faeries shoot some video.  GO and check out the clips on their site, they're supercool.
<br>
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kalannar] I am the user interface programmer for Origin
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Medwynd the interface is it going to be customizable?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] More than you can imagine.
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kalannar] It is going to be extremely customizable
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Kalannar] You should be able to decide how much room it will take up on your screen
<br>
<br><b>[Talebearer]</b> Medwynd, you have much experience in the MMORPG field?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Talebearer] I have worked on quite a few MUD's, implementing many things from ranged combat to spell systems to celestial occurances, but this is my first professional gig on a mmorpg
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Hyperion what do you do for the team?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Hyperion is the guy who does the skies and whatnot.
<br>
<br><b>[cannis]</b> Ubiq-is cheating on the game, going to be a problem, or do you think that you have eliminated to where someone couldn't cheat
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> cannis] players will always find the shortest path to the cheese.  We have a lot of experience which allows us to make -less- cheatable systems
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> And plug a lot of holes, but some will likely sneak through.  And when they do, Tyrant will be there, like the hammer of god.
<br>
<br><b>[Kaladon]</b> Hyperion....will we beable to look up and click on a star to learn its name and info about it... like who named it?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kaladon] not likely.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Shadex]</b> Ubiq: I am sorry if I missed your response to the voice recognition question... Yay or nay?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Shadex] voice recognition?  As in Dragon Diction?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Not at launch, anyway.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Unless it works naturally without help from us =)
<br>
<br><b>[Kalannar]</b> Ubiq is there going to be one currency like gold or multiple ones?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Kalannar] one currency. 
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Talyn]</b> Ubiq: Could you expand a little on the name filter and what type of names we can have?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Talyn] I already did. =)
<br>
<br><b>[ZEO-is-watching-b-bots]</b> ubiq] think you are more famous then battlebots?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zeo] not even close.
<br>
<br><b>[Dethfyre]</b> (Reasked question, feel free to ignore) Is there any way with what you have planned to have large battles (Not like 10 on 10, but _wars_). 
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Dethfyre] We'll see.  The limitation is polys on screen, but our LOD technology is very good.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> So wars may be possible but not pretty.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Or they may be so laggy and poly heavy that they just aren't any fun.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Talyn]</b> Ubiq: Will the best way to fight be in heavy plate, or can I fight in clothes and still kick @$$?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Talyn] You'll have different advantages and disadvantages if you spend your ankhs in that manner.  You'll likely do more damage, but take more damage as well.
<br>
<br><b>[Dethfyre]</b> What would you say the upper limit would be for a person on a 56k? (People on screen)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Dethfyre] it depends on what those people are doing.
<br><b>[Dethfyre]</b> How about fighthing (And, yeah, I know netcode isn't close to finalized)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Dethfyre] fighting is problematic, lots of action going on around you.  If we've done our job right, you'll see the people around you moving smoothly
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> and people farther away will be jerkier, since you theoretically care less about them.
<br>
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> I'm wondering if fighting in this game will be more realistic.. I mean, swining a gigantic battle axe at an ogre and missing?  How is that possible when their beer belly is right in your face!?!?
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> swinging, rather
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Baastuul] combat systems are abstractions. =)  Remember, the point isn't necessarily realism but fun.
<br><b>[Baastuul]</b> ubiq]  IMHO, it isnt fun seeing your character swing his sword at an ogre and continually miss :)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Baastuul] true, but one-hit kills are not fun for the recipient of the kill, and we need to use the same system for monsters that we do for playrs.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Talyn]</b> Ubiq: will heavy armor restrict moves, I don't want people doing flips and karate kicks in plate mail
<br><b></b>[Ubiq]</b> Talyn] hadn't thought about it to be honest.
<br>
<br><b>[Dethfyre]</b> LOL, next question :)  How much will players be able to alter the landscape?  For instance if I find the perfect place to build a house (when implemented), except for the fact that there's a tree there, will I be able to sing "I'm a lumberjack" and get rid of it?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Dethfyre] If we did that, our landscape would be a barren, treeless plain inside of a week.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Benjamyn]</b> personally i dont think mages should be able to wear plate, that is the thing i liked about EQ
<br><b>[Ubiq] Benjamyn]</b> we agree.  You will need skill to gain practical use out of armor.
<br>
<br><b>[Vandal|UO2News]</b> Ubiq - you have any character preferences so far? Gasper? Hyperion? Medwynd?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Vandal] Racially I am still unsure, but am definately going with the path of a mage
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Vandal] Mages have always held the greatest interest for me so I always try to put my 2 cents in about them
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Mazhar]</b> Can characters gain weight in Origin? and gain muscle mass? +)
<br><b>[Ubiq] Mazhar]</b> too soon to tell =)
<br>
<br><b>[Lillebusy]</b> I want to play so much my stomach hurts.
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Lillebusy]I have the client running on my machine right now if it makes you feel better :)
<br><b>[Lillebusy]</b> (Medwynd) Makes me feel worse, do you feel better?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Lillebusy]I could have told you i was walking around Buc's Den....
<br>
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> As Ubiq said, I do the whatnot... I'm one of three graphics programmers on the team. I can't comment on the design aspects of the moons.
<br>
<br><b>[Sanctum-Benjamyn]</b> Hyperion- I might have missed this question, but will there be comets and random events in the sky?
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Our data driven approach should allow us to create special game events, including the appearance of the heavens.


